---
title: "merkle_tree::node_hash (Pyth Sui Contracts)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_order: greater_than(childA, childB)
    q_order --> q_swap: true, swap(childA, childB)
    q_order --> q_build: false, keep order
    q_swap --> q_build
    q_build --> q_concat: v = [MERKLE_NODE_PREFIX] + data(childA) + data(childB)
    q_concat --> [*]: return hash(v) (keccak256 truncated to 20 bytes)

    note right of q_order
        INV-001: children are sorted (smaller first) for canonical hash
        INV-002: MERKLE_NODE_PREFIX (1) is prepended as domain separator
        INV-003: deterministic ordering prevents proof manipulation
    end note
